                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Pair the factors as differences of squares, then expand.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Let $P=(a+b+c)(a+b-c)(a-b+c)(-a+b+c)$. Pair the first two and last two factors, then expand:\n$$\\begin{align*}P&=\\big((a+b)^2-c^2\\big)\\big(c^2-(a-b)^2\\big)\\\\P&=(a^2+b^2+2ab-c^2)(-a^2-b^2+2ab+c^2)\\\\P&=4a^2b^2-(a^2+b^2-c^2)^2\\\\P&=4a^2b^2-\\big(a^4+b^4+c^4+2a^2b^2-2a^2c^2-2b^2c^2\\big)\\\\P&=2a^2b^2+2a^2c^2+2b^2c^2-a^4-b^4-c^4.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 80
      },
